---
import Pillar from '../../layouts/Pillar.astro';
import ChildGrid from '../../components/ChildGrid.astro';
import { CHILDREN } from '../../data/clusters';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';

const items = CHILDREN['basics'];
const schema = [{
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'Golf Basics: The Game Explained Without Condescension',
  description: 'Rules, scoring, handicaps, etiquette, formats and terminology — explained clearly for new golfers and anyone who never quite asked.',
  hasPart: items.map((i) => ({
    '@type': 'WebPage', name: i.title, url: new URL(i.href, SITE.url).href,
  })),
}];
---
<Pillar
  cluster="basics"
  title='Golf Basics: The Game Explained Without Condescension'
  description='Rules, scoring, handicaps, etiquette, formats and terminology — explained clearly for new golfers and anyone who never quite asked.'
  intro='Golf has an unusual amount of assumed knowledge, and an unhelpful culture around admitting you do not have it. Nothing here assumes you already know the answer.'
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="pil-prose">
      <h2>What actually stops new golfers</h2>
      <p>
        It is rarely the swing. It is not knowing where to stand, when to walk, what to write on
        the card, or what to do when the ball goes somewhere the rules have a specific opinion
        about. That uncertainty is what makes the first few rounds stressful, and it is entirely
        fixable in an afternoon of reading.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout-key">
        <p class="callout-title">The only three rules you need on day one</p>
        <p>
          Play the ball as it lies. Count every stroke, including the ones you would rather not.
          Do not hold anybody up. Everything else can be learned as it comes up, and nobody
          decent will mind.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <p>
        If you are brand new, read the scoring explainer first — it makes everything else make
        sense. If you have played a while but never got round to asking what a stroke index
        column is for, the handicap guide is the one.
      </p>
  </div>

  <ChildGrid items={items} heading="Guides in this section" />
</Pillar>

<style>
  .pil-prose { max-width: var(--w-prose); }
  .pil-prose :global(h2) { margin-top: var(--s-7); font-size: var(--fs-xl); }
  .pil-prose :global(li) { margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
  .pil-prose :global(li::marker) { color: var(--brand); }
  .pil-prose :global(.table-scroll) { max-width: var(--w-content); }
</style>
